# tools/css/cssom-instructions.py: the cost shapes of tests/test-cssom-instructions.cpp, run under callgrind at scale 1 and 4. Columns (tab separated): test, class (linear, nlogn, known-quadratic), the largest growth of the instructions from scale 1 to scale 4 (a linear shape may show up to 8.0, 2K), the largest number of instructions at scale 1, the reason. A ceiling only falls.
CssomInstructions.DistinctSetsOfADeclaration	linear	4.0	46000000	n distinct sets of a free-standing declaration: the block's index makes each one O(1), measured x3.76 from n to 4n (build host, GCC 16.2, 2026-11-02)
CssomInstructions.RepeatedSetsOfOneProperty	linear	4.1	115000000	n sets of one property replace in place and cost O(1) each, measured x3.92; the instructions are the machine's own work under callgrind, which no counter can be wrong about
CssomInstructions.InsertsIntoASheetAtRandomPlaces	nlogn	4.0	48000000	n inserts at random places of one sheet are n log n through the order-statistics list, measured x3.84; the limit of a linear shape (2K = x8) bounds it with room
CssomInstructions.ManyMutationsThenOneAskOfTheIndex	linear	3.6	660000000	n mutations of the sheets of a document and one ask of its index are one snapshot compile of each edited sheet and one index build, measured x3.40 with a fixed setup that dominates
